---
import Studio from "../../layouts/Studio.astro";
import RelatedPosts from "../../components/RelatedPosts.astro";
import { SITE, DEFAULT_OG, CALENDLY_URL, fmtDate, iso, POSTS } from "../../lib/blog.mjs";
import { coverBase, coverSrcset, COVER_SIZES_POST } from "../../lib/images.mjs";

const slug = "ai-website-builder-vs-developer-india";
const idx = POSTS.findIndex((p) => p.slug === slug);
const post = POSTS[idx];

const canonical = `${SITE}/blog/${slug}/`;
const ogImage = post.coverImage ? `${SITE}${post.coverImage}` : DEFAULT_OG;
const primaryTag = post.tags[0] || "Notes";
const readMins = post.readMins;
const showUpdated = post.updatedDate && +new Date(post.updatedDate) > +new Date(post.pubDate);
const updatedLabel = showUpdated ? `Updated ${fmtDate(post.updatedDate)}` : null;

const jsonld = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "BlogPosting",
      "@id": `${canonical}#post`,
      headline: post.title,
      description: post.description,
      datePublished: iso(post.pubDate),
      dateModified: iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate),
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Divyansh Sood", url: `${SITE}/`, "@id": `${SITE}/#person` },
      publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "@id": `${SITE}/#studio`,
        name: "Divyansh Sood® Studio",
        logo: { "@type": "ImageObject", url: `${SITE}/icon.svg` },
      },
      isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
      mainEntityOfPage: { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": canonical },
      image: ogImage,
      articleSection: primaryTag,
      keywords: post.tags.join(", "),
      wordCount: post.wordCount,
      timeRequired: `PT${readMins}M`,
      speakable: {
        "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
        cssSelector: [".post-title", ".post-lead"],
      },
      inLanguage: "en",
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Blog", item: `${SITE}/blog/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: post.title, item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
});
---

<Studio
  title={post.seoTitle ?? `${post.title} · Divyansh Sood`}
  description={post.description}
  canonical={canonical}
  keywords={post.tags.join(", ")}
  ogType="article"
  ogTitle={post.title}
  ogImage={ogImage}
  ogImageW={1200}
  ogImageH={750}
  articlePublished={iso(post.pubDate)}
  articleModified={iso(post.updatedDate || post.pubDate)}
  tags={post.tags}
  preloadImage={{ href: coverBase(post.coverImage), srcset: coverSrcset(post.coverImage), sizes: COVER_SIZES_POST }}
  jsonld={jsonld}
>
  <main>
    <header class="post-hero">
      <div class="post-hero-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <div class="eyebrow">
          <span>{primaryTag}</span>
          <span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span>
          {updatedLabel && <span class="post-updated">{updatedLabel}</span>}
          <span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="post-title">{post.title}</h1>
        <p class="post-lead">{post.description}</p>
        <div class="post-meta">
          <span>By Divyansh Sood</span><span>{fmtDate(post.pubDate)}</span><span>{readMins} min read</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    {post.coverImage && (
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        <figure class="post-cover">
          <img
            src={coverBase(post.coverImage)}
            srcset={coverSrcset(post.coverImage)}
            sizes={COVER_SIZES_POST}
            alt={post.coverAlt ?? post.title}
            width="1200"
            height="750"
            fetchpriority="high"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>
    )}

    <article class="wrap narrow post-body">
<p>An AI website builder will produce something that looks like a website in about four minutes. For an Indian small business weighing that against hiring a developer, the honest comparison isn't about quality of output — it's about what happens in month six.</p>
<p>I have an unusual angle here: I build websites for clients <em>and</em> I built an AI website generator — <a href="/projects/webseek/">WebSeek.ai</a>. So I know exactly what these tools do well, because I built one, and exactly where they stop.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-they-are-genuinely-good-at">What they're genuinely good at</h2>
<p>Not nothing. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Getting something online today.</strong> If you have no web presence at all, an AI-generated page beats nothing by a wide margin, immediately.</li>
<li><strong>Testing whether an idea has legs.</strong> Before committing real money to a business, a rough page to see if anyone responds is a sensible experiment.</li>
<li><strong>Getting past the blank page.</strong> Even working with a developer, arriving with a rough generated draft of what you had in mind is a genuinely useful starting point. It's often faster than describing it.</li>
</ul>
<p>If you're at that stage, use one. I'd rather you had something online than waited six months for a budget.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="where-they-stop">Where they stop</h2>
<h3 id="they-generate-a-page-not-a-funnel">They generate a page, not a funnel</h3>
<p>The output is a page that describes your business. What earns money is a path: someone arrives with a problem, is convinced you can solve it, and contacts you in the way they actually prefer — which in India is almost always WhatsApp, with the message pre-filled and the context carried across.</p>
<p>That path is a decision about your specific customers. It isn't a layout, so a generator doesn't produce it.</p>
<h3 id="nobody-arrives">Nobody arrives</h3>
<p>The biggest gap by far. A generated site is generic by construction — it doesn't know that your customers search for "Gaggal airport taxi" rather than "travel services," and it can't build the pages, structure and local signals that make you findable for those searches. <a href="/projects/baglamukhi-travels/">Baglamukhi Travels</a> averages position 5.7 on Google because the site was built around the specific searches that matter in Kangra. No generator can do that, because it doesn't know your district.</p>
<h3 id="the-second-change">The second change is where it breaks</h3>
<p>The first version arrives in minutes. Then you need a page for a new route, or a booking form that captures something specific, or your prices change across nine places. Now you're either regenerating and losing your edits, or editing code you didn't write and don't understand.</p>
<p>This is the same trap as any builder — the demo is fast and the second year is slow. It's the argument in <a href="/blog/custom-website-vs-wordpress/">custom vs WordPress</a> and <a href="/blog/own-your-stack-code-portability/">owning your stack</a>, and generated code doesn't escape it.</p>
<h3 id="it-cannot-tell-you-you-are-wrong">It can't tell you that you're wrong</h3>
<p>The most underrated part of hiring someone. A generator does exactly what you asked. It will not tell you that your homepage leads with the wrong thing, that the service you're proudest of isn't the one people search for, or that a simpler site would convert better. Ask it to do something ill-advised and it will do it well.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="the-honest-decision">The honest decision</h2>
<p><strong>Use an AI builder if</strong> you have nothing online and need something this week, you're testing whether a business idea works, your site is a business card rather than a channel, or your budget genuinely is near zero. All legitimate.</p>
<p><strong>Hire a developer if</strong> the website is meant to <em>bring</em> customers rather than confirm you exist, you need to be found for specific local searches, you have a real booking or enquiry flow, or you'll still be running this site in three years.</p>
<p>The dividing question isn't "how much does it cost." It's <strong>is this site meant to earn, or to exist?</strong> Both are valid answers. They just want completely different tools.</p>
<hr>
<h2 id="what-i-tell-people-who-ask">What I tell people who ask me directly</h2>
<p>If you're not sure the business is going to work yet — generate something, put it up, spend your money on the business instead. Come back when you have customers and the site is the constraint.</p>
<p>If you already have customers and the site isn't bringing more, a generator won't fix that, because the thing that's broken isn't the layout.</p>
<p>And if what you actually want is the AI <em>inside</em> the site — an assistant that answers from your own content, or a feature that does real work for a customer — that isn't a website generator at all. It's <a href="/services/ai-development/">AI development</a>, and it's a different job with a different answer.</p>
<hr>
<p><em>I'm Divyansh Sood, a web developer in Himachal Pradesh — I build custom-coded sites for Indian businesses, and I built an AI website generator, so I'm not guessing about either side of this. Tell me where your business actually is and <a href="https://wa.me/919816091875">WhatsApp me</a> — if the honest answer is "use a generator for now," I'll say that.</em></p>
      <div class="tags">{post.tags.map((t) => <span>{t}</span>)}</div>
    </article>

    <RelatedPosts slug={slug} audience={post.audience} />

    <section class="post-foot-cta">
      <div class="wrap narrow">
        {post.audience === "indian-smb" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something in India?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. WhatsApp reply in under an hour, 9 AM–9 PM IST — I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="https://wa.me/919816091875" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Message me on WhatsApp <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : post.audience === "d2c-brand" ? (
          <>
            <h2>Building a brand a theme can't carry?</h2>
            <p>If your store has a model that off-the-shelf builders fight — hand-numbered drops, creator commerce, premium D2C — tell me about it. I read every brief personally.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/#work">See the work</a>
            </div>
          </>
        ) : (
          <>
            <h2>Working on something similar?</h2>
            <p>If a post here matches what you're building, send me the brief. I reply personally, usually within a couple of hours — and I'll tell you within a day if it's a fit.</p>
            <div class="cta-row">
              <a class="btn btn-primary" href="mailto:hello@divyanshsood.com"
                >Email me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
              <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={CALENDLY_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
                >Book a 15-min intro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
              >
            </div>
          </>
        )}
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Studio>
